                                "sense_id": "c8c76a26-101c-3814-9591-9fa0562421d0",
                                "text": "If the kings do not come to the public supper, each of them must have two choenixes of meal and a cotyle of wine sent home to him at his house; if they come, they are given a double quantity of each, and the same when any private man invites them to his table."
